v0.17 adversarial constructor repair complete.

v0.16 was attacked before official seed freeze. Preserved residuals include:
- describe_contract typo (DENSITY_DENOMATOR);
- overbroad n-domain admitting n=3 although target 11 clauses exceeds the 8-clause finite universe, leaving a guaranteed nontermination case;
- latent nested retry-state repeat path after modulo-bias rejection;
- common-stream self-test exercised an unused namespace;
- 7/2 was labeled exact although odd-n realized density differs after rounding;
- coverage scaffold introduced size-dependent structural confounds.

Replacement primary constructor:
FIG5-clause-priority-3cnf/v0.17

Rule:
external block seed -> n-independent SHA-256 priority per canonical eligible width-3 clause -> finite bottom-m selection, where m=round_half_up((7/2)*n).

Properties:
- allowed n exactly {8,9,10,11,12,13};
- finite clause universe and finite sort; no unbounded candidate/retry loop;
- active support 1..n is required and fails closed; no seed search or clause injection repair;
- same eligible clause keeps the same priority across n;
- target density 7/2 is explicitly separated from realized odd-n density;
- no solver/verifier feedback.

Synthetic/test-only evidence:
- initial self-test: 256 synthetic seeds × 6 levels = 1,536 formulas; 0 structural failures; 0 observed priority collisions;
- widened stress: 1,000 synthetic seeds × 6 = 6,000 formulas; 0 structural failures; 0 observed priority collisions;
- 5,000 adjacent comparisons: mean exact-clause Jaccard 0.6184194319; mean old-clause retention 0.7982516484;
- independent reconstruction matched 96/96 constructions.

